From aa165eceb02d05c4e5e944550d54033c6fcdc7ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vaibhav <vgupta1192@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 07:09:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/16] Add Movies/Series toggles alongside Adult (8 configs
 total), never offer Seerr for Adult

Extends the single Adult on/off toggle from the previous commit into
three independent ones (Movies/Series/Adult), covering all 2^3 = 8
combinations. Generated rather than hand-enumerated (ALL_CONFIGS in
manifest.js) so a fourth toggle later is a small change, not a rewrite.
The all-enabled config keeps living at the root URL for backward
compatibility; every other combination gets a URL prefix naming exactly
which catalogs it includes (e.g. /movies-adult), mounted at startup
along with its own /<slug>/configure page. The configure page now shows
one checkbox per catalog and computes the resulting manifest URL
client-side.

Also: Stremio's stream/meta requests carry only a content id, never
which catalog surfaced it, so there was no way for the existing
Request-via-Seerr fallback to know an id was Adult content before
offering to submit it to Seerr (a mainstream Radarr/Sonarr-backed
request system that has no reason to receive adult content requests).
Fixed by having the catalog handler record every id it serves under the
Adult catalog into a set (populated the moment a user browses that
catalog, which necessarily happens before they could click into a title
from it) and checking that set both where the stream is built
(defineStreamHandler's buildRequestStream) and, as a second layer, at
the /request endpoint itself in server.js in case a client ever holds a
stale stream URL from before this exclusion existed.

Verified live: all 8 configs produce distinct manifest ids with exactly
the right catalogs, catalog data resolves correctly under every scoped
prefix, configure pages pre-check the right boxes per URL, and the
original root install (streams, episode lists, Adult catalog) is
unaffected.
